From 9835838e07ddc07f0888e79217762dc230fa084a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:55:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/43] acpi_battery: add the ThinkPad charge threshold logic
 and tests

ThinkPads can stop charging below 100 percent. The hotkey device of
the firmware reads the thresholds with BCTG and BCSG and sets them
with BCCS and BCSS. Add the pure logic for these methods, following
the thinkpad_acpi driver of Linux: bit 8 of a result marks support,
bit 9 individual addressing and bit 31 an error; the threshold is in
the low byte, and a stop of 0 means a full charge. The argument
carries the battery in bits 8 and 9, BAT0 being 1 and BAT1 being 2.
Other device names are not guessed.

A threshold pair is valid when stop is 1 to 100 and start is below
stop; a start of 0 leaves it to the firmware. When a new pair is set,
the start goes first if the limit is lowered, so that the start never
lies above the stop in between.

The logic has no kernel dependencies and is tested on the host.

Signed-off-by: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
(cherry picked from commit 36295c9ced45682c233b7a0b534da2f0ee8a79e2)
---
